{
    "info": {
        "_postman_id": "codemind-api-collection",
        "name": "CodeMind API",
        "description": "CodeMind v2 — AI-Powered Code Intelligence Platform\n\nArchitecture:\n- API Server: handles search, agents, graph queries, job queuing\n- Indexing Worker: standalone process that polls for pending jobs and executes indexing\n- MCP Server: exposes tools via Model Context Protocol for Claude Desktop / Cursor\n\nFeatures:\n- Repository indexing (local path + Git URL) via job queue\n- Semantic & hybrid code search\n- Autonomous LangGraph agents with playbook-based reasoning\n- SQLite graph queries (callers, callees, dependencies)\n- Catalogs for high-level repository documentation\n- System health & stats",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
    },
    "variable": [
        {
            "key": "base_url",
            "value": "http://localhost:8000",
            "description": "CodeMind server base URL"
        },
        {
            "key": "repo_id",
            "value": "c03b42a23b1fdc85",
            "description": "Default repo ID for testing (set after indexing)"
        },
        {
            "key": "job_id",
            "value": "",
            "description": "Job ID from indexing"
        },
        {
            "key": "agent_job_id",
            "value": "",
            "description": "Job ID from autonomous agent execution"
        }
    ],
    "item": [
        {
            "name": "1. Indexing",
            "description": "Index repositories from local folders or Git URLs.\n\nThe API queues a job and returns immediately. The standalone Indexing Worker picks up pending jobs and executes them.\n\nRun the worker: `python -m codemind.worker.index_worker`",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "Index Local Folder",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('job_id', jsonData.job_id);",
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('repo_id', jsonData.repo_id);",
                                    "pm.test('Index request accepted', function () {",
                                    "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                                    "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql('pending');",
                                    "});"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript"
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"repo_path\": \"/path/to/your/local/project\"\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/index",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "index"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Queue indexing for a local folder. The repo_path must be an absolute path to an existing directory.\n\nReturns job_id and repo_id immediately. The Indexing Worker will pick up this job.\nUse 'Get Job Status' to poll progress."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Index Git URL",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('job_id', jsonData.job_id);",
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('repo_id', jsonData.repo_id);",
                                    "pm.test('Index request accepted', function () {",
                                    "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                                    "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql('pending');",
                                    "});"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript"
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"repo_url\": \"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi.git\",\n  \"branch\": \"master\"\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/index",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "index"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Queue indexing for a Git repository by URL. The Worker will clone the repo locally.\n\nSupported: GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, or any Git URL.\nDefault branch: main"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "List Repositories",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/repos",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "repos"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "List all indexed repositories with metadata.\n\nResponse includes: repo_id, name, branch, path, repo_url, status, total_files, last_indexed, first_author, total_commits, last_pr_title, last_pr_user, last_pr_merged_at"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Get Job Status",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "jobs",
                                "{{job_id}}"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Poll indexing job status.\n\nStatuses:\n- pending: queued, waiting for the Indexing Worker to pick up\n- running: Worker is actively indexing\n- completed: indexing finished successfully\n- failed: indexing failed (see error field)\n\nIncludes: stage, progress (0-100), error (if failed), repo_id"
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "2. Search",
            "description": "Search indexed codebases using semantic vectors or hybrid (vector + graph) modes.",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "Semantic Search",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"query\": \"authentication functions\",\n  \"repo_id\": \"{{repo_id}}\",\n  \"search_mode\": \"semantic\",\n  \"limit\": 10\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/search",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "search"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Pure semantic search using embedding vectors.\n\nReturns: chunk_text, file_path, start_line, score (0-1, higher is better), context (classes/functions)"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Hybrid Search with Filters",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"query\": \"API endpoints\",\n  \"repo_id\": \"{{repo_id}}\",\n  \"search_mode\": \"hybrid\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"file_types\": [\".py\"],\n    \"file_patterns\": [\"api\", \"routes\"],\n    \"exclude_patterns\": [\"test_\"]\n  },\n  \"limit\": 10\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/search",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "search"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Hybrid search combining semantic vectors with structural filters.\n\nAvailable filters:\n- file_types: list of extensions [\".py\", \".ts\"]\n- file_patterns: filter by path patterns\n- class_names: filter by class names\n- exclude_patterns: exclude paths matching patterns"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Structural Search",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"query\": \"graph related code\",\n  \"repo_id\": \"{{repo_id}}\",\n  \"search_mode\": \"structural\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"file_types\": [\".py\"],\n    \"class_names\": [\"SQLiteGraphAdapter\"]\n  },\n  \"limit\": 5\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/search",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "search"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Pure structural search — graph-only, no semantic matching.\n\nReturns files matching the structural filters without vector similarity."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Search by Symbol",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"query\": \"PlannerAgent class\",\n  \"repo_id\": \"{{repo_id}}\",\n  \"search_mode\": \"semantic\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"symbol_type\": \"class\"\n  },\n  \"limit\": 5\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/search",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "search"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Search for specific code symbols (classes, functions, methods)."
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "3. Autonomous Agents",
            "description": "LangGraph-powered autonomous agents that use Think→Act→Observe loops with playbook-based reasoning.\n\nWorkflow:\n1. POST to start agent → returns job_id\n2. GET status to poll progress\n3. GET result when completed\n\nAlso includes direct playbook execution for simpler, specialized tasks.",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "Direct Playbook Execution",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"playbook_name\": \"code_explorer\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Explain how the authentication flow works in this repository\",\n  \"repo_id\": \"{{repo_id}}\"\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/agents/playbook",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "agents",
                                "playbook"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Execute a specific playbook directly and synchronously.\n\nplaybook_name: name of the playbook (e.g. code_explorer, catalog_generator, catalog_search) or 'auto' for automatic selection based on prompt.\nprompt: the input for the playbook.\nrepo_id: (optional) scope the analysis to a specific repository."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Execute Agent - Architecture Analysis",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('agent_job_id', jsonData.job_id);",
                                    "pm.test('Agent started', function () {",
                                    "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                                    "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql('pending');",
                                    "});"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript"
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"goal\": \"Generate a detailed high-level architecture diagram with Mermaid\",\n  \"repo_id\": \"{{repo_id}}\",\n  \"max_iterations\": 10,\n  \"allowed_playbooks\": null\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/agents/autonomous",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "agents",
                                "autonomous"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Start an autonomous agent with a natural language goal.\n\nThe agent uses Think→Act→Observe loops:\n- Selects the best playbook (e.g. code_analyzer)\n- Auto-finishes after sufficient data gathering\n- Runs asynchronously\n\nmax_iterations: caps the planner loop (default: 10)\nallowed_playbooks: restrict to specific playbooks (null = all)"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Execute Agent - Documentation",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('agent_job_id', jsonData.job_id);",
                                    "pm.test('Agent started', function () {",
                                    "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                                    "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql('pending');",
                                    "});"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript"
                            }
